   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "NEW · THE PAST PARTICIPLE (FORM 3)",
    "html": "Every verb has <b>3 forms</b>:<br><b>1 · Base</b> (the dictionary): <i>visit</i><br><b>2 · Past Simple</b> (you know it!): <i>visited</i><br><b>3 · Past participle</b> (new!): <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span><br><br>Today we learn <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>FORM 3</b></span>. In Portuguese, it is like <i>visitado, comido, visto</i>.<br>💡 Step by step: first the <b>regular</b> verbs, then the <b>irregular</b> verbs."
   }
  },
