  {
   "key": "pp-context",
   "title": "Present Perfect · from the Past Simple (context)",
   "tags": {
    "content": [
     "Present Perfect",
     "Past Simple"
    ],
    "levels": [
     "A2"
    ],
    "skills": [
     "Leitura"
    ]
   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "NEW TENSE · THE PRESENT PERFECT",
    "html": "You know the <b>Past Simple</b>:<br><i>I <b>visited</b> Rio last year. · She <b>visited</b> Rio in 2020.</i><br><br>Now the <b>Present Perfect</b>, with the same verb:<br><i>I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio. · She <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.</i><br><br>💡 Look: no <i>last year</i>, no <i>in 2020</i>. We will see why in a minute!"
   }
  },
  {
   "key": "pp-formula",
   "title": "Present Perfect · the formula (have / has + form 3)",
   "tags": {
    "content": [
     "Present Perfect"
    ],
    "levels": [
     "A2"
    ],
    "skills": [
     "Leitura"
    ]
   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "THE FORMULA",
    "html": "<b>person</b> + <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>HAVE</b></span> / <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>HAS</b></span> + <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>FORM 3</b></span><br><br>Colors: <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>HAVE</b></span> = I, you, we, they · <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>HAS</b></span> = he, she, it · <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>FORM 3</b></span> = past participle<br><br>⚠️ he / she / it → <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span>, like <i>he work<b>s</b></i>, <i>she ha<b>s</b></i>.<br>⚠️ Always <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>form 3</b></span>: ✗ <i>I have visit</i> ✗ <i>I have ate</i> ✓ <i>I have eaten</i>"
   }
  },
