  {
   "key": "pp-vs-ps",
   "title": "Present Perfect × Past Simple · when or no when?",
   "tags": {
    "content": [
     "Present Perfect",
     "Past Simple"
    ],
    "levels": [
     "A2"
    ],
    "skills": [
     "Leitura"
    ]
   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "PAST SIMPLE OR PRESENT PERFECT?",
    "html": "Did you say <b>WHEN</b>? → <b>Past Simple</b><br><i>I <b>visited</b> Rio <b>in 2019</b>. · She <b>visited</b> Rio <b>last year</b>.</i><br>WHEN words: <i>yesterday, last week, last year, in 2019, 3 years ago, when I was a child</i><br><br>No WHEN, only the <b>experience</b>? → <b>Present Perfect</b><br><i>I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio. · She <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.</i><br><br>⚠️ ✗ <i>I have visited Rio in 2019.</i> → ✓ <i>I visited Rio in 2019.</i>"
   }
  },
